  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Text was hand set at Stamperia Valdonega. The first poem has been printed at Wild Carrot Letterpress, the second poem printed at Stamperia Valdonega, and the last poem at Heritage Printers ... The lithographs were printed at Trestle Editions ... The design is by Benjamin Shiff ... This edition consists of three presentations. The first being seven hundred and fifty bound copies, numbered 1-750, signed on the colophon by the artist and the poet. The second consists of fifty portfolios of the lithographs without text collé to Arches paper, each lithograph signed by the artist and numbered 1/50-50/50. The third consists of twenty portfolios having the complete text printed on Arches, the lithographs collé to the sheet bearing the appropriate facing text, with each sheet containing a lithograph signed by the artist and numbered I/XX-XX/XX"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Spanish text printed in red; parallel English text in black. Some ill. on blue, red or gold paper; one ill. on red paper, mounted on cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Signed by the author and the artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in drop-back box.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Nocturno de San Ildefonso = San Ildefonso nocturne -- Vuelta = Return -- Piel, sonido del mundo = Skin, sound of the world.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">RBC copy: No. 187 [of the first presentation]. Binding: buckram; housed in matching drop-back box. Presented by James R. and Mary M. Patton.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
